\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par  \cf0 1.   Man of Sorrows! Wondrous Name
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0  For the Son of God, who came
\par  Ruined sinners to reclaim!
\par  Hallelujah! what a Saviour!
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  2.  Bearing shame and scoffing rude,
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0  In my place condemned He stood,
\par  Sealed my pardon with His blood:
\par  Hallelujah! what a Saviour!
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par   3.  Guilty, vile, and helpless we;
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0  Spotless Lamb of God was He:
\par Full atonement, - can it be?
\par  Hallelujah! what a Saviour!
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  4.  Lifted up was he to die,
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0  'It is finished' was His cry;
\par Now in heaven exalted high:
\par  Hallelujah! what a Saviuour!
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5.   When He comes, our glorious King,
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0 All His ransomed home to bring,
\par Then anew this song we'll sing,
\par \pard       'Hallelujah! what a Saviour!\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

